1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,536
When Steve and I wrote,
the lobby was pretty much in charge

2
00:00:03,536 --> 00:00:06,840
of the discourse
and pretty much in charge of policy.

3
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:08,742
But that has changed.

4
00:00:08,742 --> 00:00:13,079
The West is leading
Ukraine down the primrose

5
00:00:13,079 --> 00:00:17,217
path, and the Israelis
are executing a genocide in Gaza.

6
00:00:17,283 --> 00:00:20,954
It's not China's fault
that it wants to be powerful.

7
00:00:20,987 --> 00:00:25,258
So if you get into trouble
and you dial 911,

8
00:00:25,258 --> 00:00:28,261
there's nobody at the other end.

9
00:00:28,361 --> 00:00:34,734
Hello this is John Mearsheimer, and in today's
episode, I would like to talk about

10
00:00:34,734 --> 00:00:37,737
the new book on the Israel lobby

11
00:00:37,737 --> 00:00:41,074
by Eli Clifton and Ian Lustick.

12
00:00:41,608 --> 00:00:44,477
It's called Israel's Lobby.

13
00:00:44,477 --> 00:00:48,214
America in the grip of a Foreign Power.

14
00:00:48,848 --> 00:00:51,284
I think this is a truly important book,

15
00:00:51,284 --> 00:00:54,788
and I hope that all of the viewers

16
00:00:54,854 --> 00:00:58,591
go out and buy a copy
and read it very carefully.

17
00:00:58,992 --> 00:01:01,561
Of course,
this is a subject that's dear to my heart

18
00:01:01,561 --> 00:01:04,764
because along with Steve Walt,
I wrote an article and a book

19
00:01:04,764 --> 00:01:10,637
on the subject of the Israel
lobby back in 2006 2007.

20
00:01:10,637 --> 00:01:12,038
Steve and I wrote the article,

21
00:01:12,038 --> 00:01:16,309
which appeared in the London
Review of Books in 2006.

22
00:01:16,309 --> 00:01:19,846
And then, of course,
our book came out, The Israel Lobby

23
00:01:19,846 --> 00:01:23,716
and US Foreign Policy in 2007.

24
00:01:24,217 --> 00:01:27,987
And what I'd like to do is tell you why

25
00:01:27,987 --> 00:01:31,257
I think that the new book by Eli

26
00:01:31,257 --> 00:01:34,694
Clifton and Ian Lustick, is so important.

27
00:01:34,694 --> 00:01:39,199
And in the process,
I want to do that by comparing it to the

28
00:01:39,199 --> 00:01:41,134
book that Steve and I wrote.

29
00:01:42,569 --> 00:01:43,770
This book is not

30
00:01:43,770 --> 00:01:46,873
just an updated version
of what Steve and I wrote.

31
00:01:46,906 --> 00:01:51,244
This book has all sorts
of new insights in it

32
00:01:51,244 --> 00:01:55,215
that people should consider
very seriously.

33
00:01:55,215 --> 00:01:59,152
And the way I'd like to proceed is,
first of all, I just like to talk

34
00:01:59,219 --> 00:02:03,323
about what
the basic arguments are in the two books.

35
00:02:03,523 --> 00:02:09,329
Then I'd like to talk about
the underlying conceptual framework

36
00:02:09,362 --> 00:02:15,201
that has to underpin
any discussion of the Israel lobby

37
00:02:15,201 --> 00:02:17,137
and of course, underpins both

38
00:02:17,137 --> 00:02:20,673
the book Steve and I wrote in the book
that Eli and Ian wrote.

39
00:02:20,940 --> 00:02:23,977
And then I want to talk about the nitty

40
00:02:24,010 --> 00:02:27,714
gritty changes that have taken place since

41
00:02:27,814 --> 00:02:32,952
2006, 2007
that, of course, heavily inform

42
00:02:33,186 --> 00:02:37,757
this new book called 
Israel's Lobby.

43
00:02:38,324 --> 00:02:42,529
Let me just start off
with the core arguments.

44
00:02:42,862 --> 00:02:46,166
Both of us or both books argue

45
00:02:46,199 --> 00:02:50,603
that there is an Israel lobby
that is very powerful.

46
00:02:50,737 --> 00:02:55,775
Now, it's very important to emphasize that
in both books, the authors

47
00:02:55,808 --> 00:03:02,315
go to great lengths to make it clear that
this is not a Jewish lobby by any means.

48
00:03:02,315 --> 00:03:04,450
It's an Israel lobby.

49
00:03:04,450 --> 00:03:10,657
Not all Jews by any means
belong to the Israel lobby.

50
00:03:10,657 --> 00:03:14,561
And the Israel and the Israel lobby,
of course, includes

51
00:03:14,561 --> 00:03:18,765
many non-Jews,
Christian Zionists, for example.

52
00:03:18,765 --> 00:03:22,669
So this is not the Jewish lobby,
it's the Israel lobby.

53
00:03:23,269 --> 00:03:28,308
Now, the argument that Steve
and I made the principal argument

54
00:03:28,641 --> 00:03:34,314
was that the lobby is bad
for American foreign policy.

55
00:03:34,714 --> 00:03:37,717
It's bad for a strategic point of view.

56
00:03:37,717 --> 00:03:40,720
And from a moral point of view.

57
00:03:40,787 --> 00:03:47,627
And in the absence of the lobby,
the United States, we argued, would have

58
00:03:47,694 --> 00:03:52,765
a very different foreign policy,
especially in the Middle East.

59
00:03:53,199 --> 00:03:56,769
We did not say

60
00:03:56,769 --> 00:04:00,073
much in our written work

61
00:04:00,139 --> 00:04:03,276
about the importance

62
00:04:03,276 --> 00:04:06,646
of the lobby for Israel.

63
00:04:07,513 --> 00:04:12,051
Nor did we say much about the importance

64
00:04:12,051 --> 00:04:16,589
of the lobby
for the American Jewish community.

65
00:04:17,657 --> 00:04:20,193
Nor did we say much,

66
00:04:20,193 --> 00:04:24,430
if anything, about the impact
that the lobby has

67
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:27,867
on American liberal democracy

68
00:04:27,934 --> 00:04:31,971
or on American political institutions.

69
00:04:32,405 --> 00:04:35,408
But it's important to understand

70
00:04:35,408 --> 00:04:41,214
that the book by Eli Clifton
and Ian Lustig

71
00:04:41,547 --> 00:04:44,550
not only argues that

72
00:04:44,684 --> 00:04:47,687
the lobby is bad
for American foreign policy.

73
00:04:47,687 --> 00:04:50,690
It is that it's bad for Israel.

74
00:04:50,890 --> 00:04:56,396
It argues that it's bad for American Jews,
and very importantly,

75
00:04:56,429 --> 00:05:00,300
it argues that it now is in a position
where it's

76
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:04,370
undermining,
undermining liberal democracy.

77
00:05:04,404 --> 00:05:10,810
So the charge in the new book
is much broader

78
00:05:10,977 --> 00:05:14,347
than the charge in the book
that Steve and I wrote.

79
00:05:15,348 --> 00:05:19,752
Now, what about the underlying
conceptual framework?

80
00:05:20,186 --> 00:05:23,189
Anytime you think about the lobby,

81
00:05:23,189 --> 00:05:28,027
you have to think about its influence
on the discourse.

82
00:05:28,194 --> 00:05:32,131
This is the discourse about Israel,
the discourse

83
00:05:32,131 --> 00:05:37,470
about the US-Israeli relationship
and the discourse about the lobby itself.

84
00:05:38,471 --> 00:05:41,808
So the question

85
00:05:41,808 --> 00:05:45,311
is, how does the lobby influence
that discourse?

86
00:05:45,712 --> 00:05:48,915
Then there's the issue of actual policy.

87
00:05:48,948 --> 00:05:52,919
And the question is
how does the lobby influence policy,

88
00:05:53,219 --> 00:05:58,891
which is different from the question of
how does the lobby influence discourse?

89
00:05:59,492 --> 00:06:02,228
Now, our argument

90
00:06:02,228 --> 00:06:08,468
back in 2006, 2007 was that the lobby

91
00:06:08,534 --> 00:06:14,474
did a very effective job at, in effect,
controlling the discourse.

92
00:06:14,474 --> 00:06:15,908
Or if you want to put it in slightly

93
00:06:15,908 --> 00:06:20,046
different words,
policing the discourse on Israel.

94
00:06:20,646 --> 00:06:23,716
And we described in

95
00:06:23,716 --> 00:06:26,719
great detail how The Lobby did that.

96
00:06:26,919 --> 00:06:30,590
We tried to account for the success
that the lobby

97
00:06:30,656 --> 00:06:35,361
had had up to that point
in managing the discourse

98
00:06:35,361 --> 00:06:39,999
in ways that were favorable
from the lobby's perspective.

99
00:06:40,533 --> 00:06:44,971
And with regard to policy,
there was just no question

100
00:06:45,004 --> 00:06:48,007
that the lobby had a

101
00:06:48,007 --> 00:06:51,110
hammerlock on US Middle East policy.

102
00:06:51,177 --> 00:06:54,247
This is not to say
it got its way every time, but

103
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:56,883
it got its way almost every time.

104
00:06:56,883 --> 00:07:00,987
And oftentimes when it didn't get its way,
it ended up

105
00:07:01,187 --> 00:07:04,190
forcing the administration

106
00:07:04,791 --> 00:07:06,926
to change its policy

107
00:07:06,926 --> 00:07:10,229
to accommodate Israel and the lobby.

108
00:07:10,296 --> 00:07:13,433
So the basic argument
that Steve and I made

109
00:07:13,433 --> 00:07:18,004
was that the lobby was very successful
in terms of controlling the discourse,

110
00:07:18,004 --> 00:07:22,642
policing the discourse,
and certainly in terms of influencing

111
00:07:22,975 --> 00:07:28,881
policy in ways that the lobby wanted
that policy to go.

112
00:07:29,248 --> 00:07:31,884
Now, the argument

113
00:07:31,884 --> 00:07:36,289
in the Clifton
Lustig book is very different.

114
00:07:36,389 --> 00:07:41,327
There is that the lobby has lost

115
00:07:41,327 --> 00:07:44,330
its ability to control the discourse,

116
00:07:44,630 --> 00:07:47,166
but it has not lost

117
00:07:47,166 --> 00:07:51,237
its ability to control policy.

118
00:07:52,104 --> 00:07:57,009
So you see the fundamental change
between our book

119
00:07:57,009 --> 00:08:00,913
and their book,
and it has to do with the discourse.

120
00:08:01,247 --> 00:08:04,550
Let me give you a sense of how I see

121
00:08:04,550 --> 00:08:07,720
the discourse having changed

122
00:08:08,554 --> 00:08:12,492
since we wrote the book back in 2007.

123
00:08:12,792 --> 00:08:18,598
And the article, of course, before
that, in 2006, when we wrote the book,

124
00:08:18,698 --> 00:08:24,604
it was almost impossible
to talk about dual loyalty.

125
00:08:24,604 --> 00:08:27,773
And if you did talk about dual loyalty,

126
00:08:27,773 --> 00:08:32,245
you had to deal with it very carefully,
very gingerly.

127
00:08:32,478 --> 00:08:37,884
It was a remarkably hot topic.

128
00:08:38,951 --> 00:08:40,586
If you look at

129
00:08:40,586 --> 00:08:45,858
the discourse today, people
not only talk about individuals

130
00:08:45,858 --> 00:08:50,162
having dual loyalty,
they talk about Israel Firsters

131
00:08:50,730 --> 00:08:53,766
the term Israel Firster, in other words,

132
00:08:53,766 --> 00:08:56,802
someone who privileges Israel's interests

133
00:08:56,836 --> 00:09:00,973
over America's interest is a term
that's used all the time.

134
00:09:00,973 --> 00:09:06,012
In fact, many prominent American Jews
who are

135
00:09:06,412 --> 00:09:09,916
pro-Israel
are referred to as Israel firsters.

136
00:09:10,416 --> 00:09:14,987
This was not an argument anyone,
including Steven and I would want to make.

137
00:09:15,054 --> 00:09:19,292
In 2006 or 2007.

138
00:09:19,292 --> 00:09:23,429
But the discourse has changed to the point
where you can make

139
00:09:23,429 --> 00:09:27,133
that argument to take
what's going on in Gaza.

140
00:09:27,199 --> 00:09:31,003
The lobby and Israel have gone
to enormous lengths to say that

141
00:09:31,003 --> 00:09:32,805
this is not a genocide.

142
00:09:32,805 --> 00:09:36,008
What the Israelis are doing

143
00:09:36,008 --> 00:09:39,412
in Gaza against the Palestinians,

144
00:09:39,679 --> 00:09:42,548
a center for Jewish Studies

145
00:09:42,548 --> 00:09:47,053
at Brandeis,
just recently released a report that shows

146
00:09:47,053 --> 00:09:50,056
that 74% of college

147
00:09:50,056 --> 00:09:54,160
students, 74% of college students,
think that

148
00:09:54,193 --> 00:09:57,196
what Israel is doing in Gaza

149
00:09:57,196 --> 00:10:00,199
against the Palestinians is a genocide.

150
00:10:00,232 --> 00:10:01,567
This is remarkable.

151
00:10:01,567 --> 00:10:06,205
And this is evidence
that the lobby has lost

152
00:10:06,205 --> 00:10:09,208
its ability to control the discourse.

153
00:10:09,408 --> 00:10:12,078
And of course, you see this
with people like

154
00:10:12,078 --> 00:10:15,815
Tucker Carlson
and Candace Owens and so forth and so on.

155
00:10:15,848 --> 00:10:19,885
There's just no question
that the discourse today

156
00:10:19,952 --> 00:10:23,289
is fundamentally different than it was in

157
00:10:23,322 --> 00:10:26,325
2006, 2007.

158
00:10:26,592 --> 00:10:30,896
Now, with regard to policy,

159
00:10:30,930 --> 00:10:35,067
there's no question, as Ian or

160
00:10:35,067 --> 00:10:40,139
Ian and Eli make clear, that that the lobby

161
00:10:40,172 --> 00:10:44,243
still has a stranglehold on U.S.

162
00:10:44,243 --> 00:10:45,711
Middle East policy.

163
00:10:46,879 --> 00:10:49,315
And the issue that they raise,

164
00:10:49,315 --> 00:10:52,752
of course,
which is a fascinating issue, is

165
00:10:54,020 --> 00:10:55,988
whether or not

166
00:10:55,988 --> 00:10:58,457
and I'll talk more about this at the end.

167
00:10:58,457 --> 00:11:02,028
You can sustain a situation
where Israel loses

168
00:11:02,028 --> 00:11:05,031
control the discourse
and people in the public domain

169
00:11:05,031 --> 00:11:12,004
talk about Israel in ways that are at odds
with policy toward Israel.

170
00:11:12,071 --> 00:11:15,808
In other words, it's very hard
to have a special relationship with Israel

171
00:11:15,875 --> 00:11:20,913
where you give Israel
unconditional support when so many people

172
00:11:20,913 --> 00:11:24,150
in the body populace have a negative view,

173
00:11:24,350 --> 00:11:27,353
a hostile view, in many cases of Israel.

174
00:11:27,386 --> 00:11:33,559
So the story that Ian and Eli are telling

175
00:11:33,559 --> 00:11:36,829
is that the discourse has changed
fundamentally

176
00:11:36,929 --> 00:11:41,133
since when Steve and I wrote a book,
but the policy has not.

177
00:11:41,467 --> 00:11:45,371
Now let's talk about the specifics.

178
00:11:45,538 --> 00:11:48,541
Let's talk about

179
00:11:48,841 --> 00:11:52,111
what has actually happened

180
00:11:52,378 --> 00:11:55,114
to change the discourse.

181
00:11:55,114 --> 00:11:58,551
And then let's then switch gears

182
00:11:58,551 --> 00:12:02,888
and talk about how the lobby has reacted

183
00:12:03,322 --> 00:12:07,393
to this deteriorating situation
from their point of view,

184
00:12:07,393 --> 00:12:10,963
in terms of the discourse,
how the lobby is reacting to that,

185
00:12:10,963 --> 00:12:14,366
and how the lobby is working
overtime today

186
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:17,970
to make sure that it maintains

187
00:12:18,137 --> 00:12:23,008
its profound influence on U.S.

188
00:12:23,008 --> 00:12:24,477
Middle East policy.

189
00:12:24,477 --> 00:12:28,681
In other words,
that the United States remains firmly

190
00:12:28,681 --> 00:12:32,451
committed
to giving Israel unconditional support.

191
00:12:32,485 --> 00:12:35,654
What is what is
what is the lobby, Israel's

192
00:12:35,654 --> 00:12:39,358
lobby, doing today to ensure that happens?

193
00:12:39,391 --> 00:12:42,928
So let's just start by talking
about what has changed.

194
00:12:42,928 --> 00:12:45,364
And here we're focusing on the discourse.

195
00:12:45,364 --> 00:12:49,635
At the risk of sounding
like engaged in self-promotion,

196
00:12:49,635 --> 00:12:53,973
I do think Steve and I, with our article
and with our book,

197
00:12:54,073 --> 00:12:59,979
played a key role
in opening up the discourse on Israel.

198
00:13:00,012 --> 00:13:03,082
Of course,
there were all sorts of other people

199
00:13:03,082 --> 00:13:07,286
who wrote before us
and after us who helped in that endeavor.

200
00:13:07,286 --> 00:13:12,892
But I think there's no question that 
the discourse

201
00:13:12,892 --> 00:13:17,730
was helped by our article
and then by our book.

202
00:13:18,030 --> 00:13:21,433
And I would marry this

203
00:13:21,467 --> 00:13:24,470
to the coming of the internet.

204
00:13:24,537 --> 00:13:28,874
The internet has been a huge problem
for Israel.

205
00:13:28,874 --> 00:13:33,179
And what's going on here
is that in the past,

206
00:13:33,179 --> 00:13:38,684
before the coming of the internet,
almost everybody relied

207
00:13:38,717 --> 00:13:46,325
on the mainstream media for their news
about the Middle East, for their news

208
00:13:46,325 --> 00:13:51,197
about Israel, for their news
about the US Israeli relationship.

209
00:13:51,197 --> 00:13:54,667
And there's no question
the lobby had a profound influence

210
00:13:54,767 --> 00:13:57,736
on what was said in the mainstream media.

211
00:13:57,770 --> 00:14:03,475
But with the coming of the internet,
you have the growth

212
00:14:03,509 --> 00:14:07,379
of all sorts of platforms,

213
00:14:08,013 --> 00:14:12,852
the growth of an alternative media
and alternative to the mainstream media,

214
00:14:13,219 --> 00:14:18,190
where it's possible to say things
that are critical of Israel,

215
00:14:18,257 --> 00:14:22,194
to post videos
of what Israel is doing in Gaza,

216
00:14:22,194 --> 00:14:27,566
which is guaranteed
to make Israel look bad and

217
00:14:28,634 --> 00:14:29,835
guaranteed to

218
00:14:29,835 --> 00:14:33,772
change the discourse on Israel.

219
00:14:33,873 --> 00:14:36,642
The US Israel relationship
and on the lobby itself.

220
00:14:36,642 --> 00:14:40,012
So one cannot underestimate

221
00:14:40,012 --> 00:14:44,917
the importance of the internet,
the importance of platforms

222
00:14:44,917 --> 00:14:49,788
like TikTok, of YouTube, of Substack

223
00:14:49,855 --> 00:14:53,959
for allowing criticism of Israel

224
00:14:54,059 --> 00:14:57,796
and the US Israeli relationship
and the lobby itself

225
00:14:57,930 --> 00:15:03,569
to percolate out into the discourse,
the mainstream discourse.

226
00:15:04,637 --> 00:15:07,840
So the internet has really mattered.

227
00:15:08,507 --> 00:15:13,879
What's also really mattered,
obviously, is Israeli behavior.

228
00:15:13,879 --> 00:15:17,549
And Clifton and Lustig

229
00:15:17,549 --> 00:15:20,753
are really good on this whole issue.

230
00:15:20,753 --> 00:15:23,756
And in fact, they have a chapter

231
00:15:24,356 --> 00:15:26,792
on Israel as a crazy state

232
00:15:26,792 --> 00:15:30,596
that everybody should read very carefully.

233
00:15:30,996 --> 00:15:34,733
But what's going on here?

234
00:15:34,767 --> 00:15:39,338
First of all, as a result of October
7th, 2023,

235
00:15:39,438 --> 00:15:42,841
Israel set out

236
00:15:42,841 --> 00:15:45,911
to expel the Palestinians from Gaza,

237
00:15:45,911 --> 00:15:50,215
and in the process,
it ended up executing a genocide.

238
00:15:50,215 --> 00:15:55,888
And this was a genocide
that virtually everybody on the planet

239
00:15:55,921 --> 00:15:59,692
watched on the internet.

240
00:15:59,692 --> 00:16:05,798
It was perfectly obvious
what the Israelis were doing.

241
00:16:05,898 --> 00:16:09,635
And furthermore, a discourse began

242
00:16:09,635 --> 00:16:15,374
to open up about Israeli policy
towards the Palestinians over time.

243
00:16:15,708 --> 00:16:19,878
This is a discourse that hardly
anybody in the public knew about.

244
00:16:19,912 --> 00:16:24,049
But it became clear to all sorts of people
that if you looked at his

245
00:16:24,083 --> 00:16:27,987
looked at Israeli behavior
towards the Palestinians over time,

246
00:16:28,554 --> 00:16:33,492
at least going back to 1948,
when the state of Israel was created,

247
00:16:33,559 --> 00:16:37,229
that the Israelis often treated

248
00:16:37,229 --> 00:16:41,567
the Palestinians
in absolutely horrible ways.

249
00:16:41,734 --> 00:16:44,937
And then, of course,
you've got a genocide on top of that.

250
00:16:44,970 --> 00:16:49,441
So I think if you look at
what the Israelis were doing.

251
00:16:49,508 --> 00:16:52,378
Not just in Gaza, but beyond Gaza.

252
00:16:52,378 --> 00:16:55,347
If you look at what they're doing
in the West Bank today,

253
00:16:55,414 --> 00:17:01,587
it's hard
not to be super critical of Israel.

254
00:17:01,587 --> 00:17:03,889
And this,
of course, is exactly what happened.

255
00:17:03,889 --> 00:17:07,259
You want to remember,
I said that this Brandeis Center

256
00:17:07,459 --> 00:17:11,230
did a survey
that showed that 74% of college students

257
00:17:11,230 --> 00:17:14,767
think that Israel
is committing a genocide in Gaza.

258
00:17:14,800 --> 00:17:18,670
There's a reason for this,
and that is that I am sure

259
00:17:18,737 --> 00:17:22,975
most of those students have watched
what's happening in Gaza

260
00:17:23,308 --> 00:17:27,880
and read about what's happening in Gaza
on TikTok

261
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:32,818
or YouTube or Substack,
and this is a huge problem for Israel.

262
00:17:32,851 --> 00:17:38,724
So what I'm saying here is that it's
really behavior coupled with the internet,

263
00:17:38,724 --> 00:17:42,161
that has really changed

264
00:17:42,161 --> 00:17:45,531
how people think and talk about Israel.

265
00:17:45,697 --> 00:17:48,567
Now, to take this a step further

266
00:17:48,567 --> 00:17:54,273
in this chapter on Israel
as a crazy state,

267
00:17:54,506 --> 00:18:00,379
Ian and Eli
tell a very interesting story about this

268
00:18:00,379 --> 00:18:06,218
whole concept of a crazy state,
and they link it very carefully to Israel.

269
00:18:06,652 --> 00:18:10,022
When I was young,
when I was a graduate student,

270
00:18:10,022 --> 00:18:13,125
there was a book that most of my fellow

271
00:18:13,158 --> 00:18:18,897
IR students read by an Israeli
called Yehezkel Dror,

272
00:18:18,897 --> 00:18:22,000
and it dealt
with the subject of crazy states.

273
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:23,669
I believe that was the title of the book.

274
00:18:23,669 --> 00:18:29,575
Crazy States, if my memory is correct,
and Dror who was an Israeli.

275
00:18:29,608 --> 00:18:34,880
Of course, his basic argument was that
there are some states in the system

276
00:18:35,180 --> 00:18:40,252
that have almost unlimited goals,

277
00:18:40,752 --> 00:18:44,089
unlimited aggressive goals,

278
00:18:44,089 --> 00:18:47,493
and they're willing to employ

279
00:18:47,493 --> 00:18:50,996
almost any means, no matter how barbaric,

280
00:18:51,196 --> 00:18:55,734
to achieve those unlimited goals.

281
00:18:55,734 --> 00:18:58,804
And of course, the canonical case here

282
00:18:58,804 --> 00:19:01,807
was Nazi Germany.

283
00:19:01,840 --> 00:19:05,811
And the argument was,
and it was not a difficult argument

284
00:19:05,811 --> 00:19:09,681
to make, was that Nazi Germany

285
00:19:09,681 --> 00:19:13,452
had extremely ambitious goals.

286
00:19:13,752 --> 00:19:19,658
They were horrible goals,
they were aggressive goals,

287
00:19:19,658 --> 00:19:24,196
and they were willing to employ
the most horrendous

288
00:19:24,363 --> 00:19:28,634
or barbaric means to achieve those goals.

289
00:19:28,967 --> 00:19:33,038
And as Lustig and Clifton pointed out,

290
00:19:33,672 --> 00:19:40,078
the purpose of Dror's book was

291
00:19:41,213 --> 00:19:44,816
to make the argument that the Arab states

292
00:19:44,883 --> 00:19:50,722
surrounding Israel were crazy states,
and therefore Israel was justified

293
00:19:50,722 --> 00:19:55,694
to do almost anything it had to do to deal
with these crazy states.

294
00:19:55,727 --> 00:19:59,331
I mean, what else could Israel do
if it was surrounded by crazy states,

295
00:19:59,331 --> 00:20:03,735
but behave in the most hard

296
00:20:03,769 --> 00:20:08,840
headed and toughest possible way
with these crazy states?

297
00:20:09,007 --> 00:20:12,010
And the point that Dror

298
00:20:12,077 --> 00:20:14,880
oh, excuse me,
the point that Lustick and Clifton

299
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:19,318
are making
is that what's happened over time is it's

300
00:20:19,318 --> 00:20:24,590
not the Arab states that surround Israel
that have turned out to be crazy states.

301
00:20:24,590 --> 00:20:29,728
It's Israel itself
that's turned out to be a crazy state.

302
00:20:29,728 --> 00:20:34,433
And the argument they make
is that if you look at Israeli

303
00:20:34,499 --> 00:20:38,537
goals in the Middle East, the emphasis on

304
00:20:39,137 --> 00:20:41,506
creating a greater Israel, the emphasis

305
00:20:41,506 --> 00:20:45,110
on wrecking all of Israel's

306
00:20:45,110 --> 00:20:48,880
powerful neighbors
and so forth and so on.

307
00:20:48,880 --> 00:20:54,720
And then if you look at the means
that Israel applies

308
00:20:54,720 --> 00:20:56,955
to achieve these goals, starting

309
00:20:56,955 --> 00:21:01,293
wars, assassinating leaders and so forth
and so on.

310
00:21:01,360 --> 00:21:05,030
You see very clearly in their story
that Israel

311
00:21:05,030 --> 00:21:08,033
has become a crazy state.

312
00:21:08,267 --> 00:21:11,737
And this argument is laid out

313
00:21:11,737 --> 00:21:15,240
in considerable detail,
and it is a very powerful argument.

314
00:21:15,240 --> 00:21:18,610
And if you think about it, this behavior

315
00:21:18,810 --> 00:21:22,281
reflects how Israel acts these days.

316
00:21:22,281 --> 00:21:25,450
And of course, getting back
to what I was saying a minute ago,

317
00:21:25,450 --> 00:21:30,589
it's very clear to people who watch,

318
00:21:30,889 --> 00:21:36,795
you know, TikTok, YouTube,
who reads Substack posts and so forth

319
00:21:36,795 --> 00:21:41,300
and so on, that Israel is behaving
like a crazy state.

320
00:21:41,967 --> 00:21:46,605
And of course, once
people become aware of this,

321
00:21:46,738 --> 00:21:49,508
the discourse is going to change.

322
00:21:49,508 --> 00:21:51,510
And that's really what's happening here.

323
00:21:51,510 --> 00:21:56,048
If you look at Israeli behavior
and you marry that to the fact

324
00:21:56,048 --> 00:22:00,552
that this behavior is apparent
to so many people in the West,

325
00:22:00,552 --> 00:22:06,124
in the United States in particular, it's
hardly surprising what's going on here.

326
00:22:06,124 --> 00:22:11,029
It's hardly surprising
why Israel is losing the American public.

327
00:22:11,930 --> 00:22:17,002
They also make another
very important argument, which you hardly

328
00:22:17,035 --> 00:22:20,806
see talked about in the American media,

329
00:22:20,806 --> 00:22:24,009
which is worth saying a few words about.

330
00:22:24,209 --> 00:22:29,281
And this has to do with Israel's
sense of itself.

331
00:22:29,281 --> 00:22:32,517
It has to do with Israeli identity.

332
00:22:32,517 --> 00:22:37,856
And they point out that this is not only
about Israeli identity, it's

333
00:22:37,856 --> 00:22:42,427
also about the identity that a number of
American Jews have as well.

334
00:22:43,995 --> 00:22:47,499
And when I was younger and

335
00:22:47,766 --> 00:22:53,171
the first time I went to Israel,
which I believe was in 1978,

336
00:22:53,605 --> 00:22:59,811
I was of the belief
that Israel was striving

337
00:22:59,845 --> 00:23:03,949
to become what was referred to
at the time as a normal country.

338
00:23:04,082 --> 00:23:09,388
Israel was going to become
just another nation state.

339
00:23:09,454 --> 00:23:11,790
It's going to be closely
affiliated with the West.

340
00:23:11,790 --> 00:23:13,759
But it was a normal state.

341
00:23:13,759 --> 00:23:19,431
I remember when I went to Israel in 1978,
and somebody told me that

342
00:23:19,498 --> 00:23:24,436
when it became clear that there were
a significant number of Israeli

343
00:23:24,436 --> 00:23:30,909
prostitutes, that many Israelis thought
that was a good thing, because it showed

344
00:23:30,909 --> 00:23:34,212
that Israel was a normal country

345
00:23:34,679 --> 00:23:39,818
and it was just another nation state.

346
00:23:39,851 --> 00:23:43,655
The Jews were finally getting
their own state, much

347
00:23:43,655 --> 00:23:48,894
the way the French had their own state,
or the Japanese had their own state.

348
00:23:48,927 --> 00:23:51,296
The Jews now had their own state.

349
00:23:51,296 --> 00:23:54,766
It was just another nation
state on the planet.

350
00:23:55,467 --> 00:24:01,440
And Ian and Eli point out
that this is only one

351
00:24:01,440 --> 00:24:06,011
strand in Jewish thinking or Israeli
thinking.

352
00:24:06,044 --> 00:24:08,046
Let's talk about it in those terms.

353
00:24:08,046 --> 00:24:11,750
There's only one strand in Israeli
thinking these days.

354
00:24:11,817 --> 00:24:17,522
There's another strand and that strand,
which has a rich history,

355
00:24:17,689 --> 00:24:21,526
basically argues that Jews as a nation

356
00:24:21,526 --> 00:24:25,564
will dwell alone and will be not,

357
00:24:25,764 --> 00:24:28,934
will not be reckoned among nations.

358
00:24:29,835 --> 00:24:32,971
Just think about that rhetoric

359
00:24:33,071 --> 00:24:38,510
that Jews are not a normal nation,
and they will not.

360
00:24:38,710 --> 00:24:41,613
They will dwell alone there alone,

361
00:24:41,613 --> 00:24:44,616
and they will not be reckoned
among nations.

362
00:24:44,616 --> 00:24:47,419
This is not just the normal nation state.

363
00:24:47,419 --> 00:24:52,190
And furthermore, they point out
that part of this worldview.

364
00:24:52,557 --> 00:24:57,095
This is the opposite worldview from
the one that Israel is a normal state.

365
00:24:57,362 --> 00:25:00,298
This is saying Israel is very special.

366
00:25:00,298 --> 00:25:06,137
It will dwell alone is the whole notion
that the world is against us.

367
00:25:06,638 --> 00:25:10,909
They're out to get the Jews
and they're out to get Israel.

368
00:25:11,243 --> 00:25:14,412
And furthermore,
and this is rhetoric that they use

369
00:25:14,412 --> 00:25:17,482
in the book, the belief is,

370
00:25:17,516 --> 00:25:20,519
according to this second worldview,

371
00:25:20,519 --> 00:25:25,924
that Gentiles,
all Gentiles, are potential Nazis.

372
00:25:26,491 --> 00:25:30,395
And the point that I and Eli make

373
00:25:30,395 --> 00:25:34,132
is that if you look at survey data

374
00:25:34,399 --> 00:25:39,404
regarding what is happening
inside of Israel, it's very clear

375
00:25:39,538 --> 00:25:42,474
that this second view

376
00:25:42,474 --> 00:25:46,845
that Israel will dwell alone
and that the world is against

377
00:25:46,845 --> 00:25:50,715
Israel, has taken hold in a serious way.

378
00:25:50,715 --> 00:25:54,052
And if anything, is likely to become

379
00:25:54,052 --> 00:25:58,523
a more potent worldview in the years
ahead.

380
00:25:58,990 --> 00:26:01,993
This reminds me that I often wonder

381
00:26:02,027 --> 00:26:05,764
why the Israelis are not more concerned

382
00:26:05,997 --> 00:26:10,969
about the fact that they have alienated
so many people around the world,

383
00:26:11,069 --> 00:26:15,840
that they have done
so much damage to Israel's reputation.

384
00:26:16,274 --> 00:26:20,779
If you think about the argument
that Ian and Eli are making,

385
00:26:20,845 --> 00:26:23,748
it's perfectly understandable

386
00:26:23,748 --> 00:26:26,284
in terms of the growing strength

387
00:26:26,284 --> 00:26:31,990
of this second sense of Israeli identity,
why Israelis don't care

388
00:26:32,057 --> 00:26:37,729
very much about what others think
about their behavior because they expect

389
00:26:38,196 --> 00:26:42,934
other countries, other nation states,
other peoples to be against them.

390
00:26:43,168 --> 00:26:46,771
That's just the way the world operates.

391
00:26:47,205 --> 00:26:51,476
So the argument here is that

392
00:26:51,509 --> 00:26:54,479
what's going on is not only that

393
00:26:54,479 --> 00:26:58,550
there has been a fundamental change

394
00:26:58,650 --> 00:27:03,421
in Israel's sense of its own identity.

395
00:27:03,455 --> 00:27:07,892
And again, this bleeds over into
how many American Jews

396
00:27:08,059 --> 00:27:11,329
think about themselves
and think about Jews in the world,

397
00:27:11,329 --> 00:27:15,567
because, again, they are making
the argument that this line of argument

398
00:27:15,567 --> 00:27:20,171
has affected
some American Jews as well as Israelis.

399
00:27:20,171 --> 00:27:24,442
So you have this phenomenon
taking place at the same time.

400
00:27:24,442 --> 00:27:30,215
Israel is behaving in barbaric ways
in places like Gaza and the West Bank.

401
00:27:30,215 --> 00:27:35,153
And this is all taking place
in the age of the internet.

402
00:27:35,153 --> 00:27:39,457
And as a result of all these factors.

403
00:27:39,491 --> 00:27:43,595
What has happened here is that Israel's

404
00:27:44,729 --> 00:27:47,132
situation, in terms of

405
00:27:47,132 --> 00:27:50,802
the discourse has badly deteriorated.

406
00:27:51,036 --> 00:27:55,774
The idea that most Americans

407
00:27:55,774 --> 00:28:01,780
have a favorable view of Israel
and a favorable view of the U.S.

408
00:28:01,813 --> 00:28:06,051
Israeli relationship,
which is what existed when Steve

409
00:28:06,051 --> 00:28:10,488
and I wrote our article
and then our book has drastically changed,

410
00:28:10,488 --> 00:28:13,491
and most Americans now

411
00:28:13,491 --> 00:28:16,494
have a negative view of Israel.

412
00:28:16,695 --> 00:28:20,699
And if anything, this is likely to change,

413
00:28:20,732 --> 00:28:25,870
certainly,
given that Israel, according to Lustick

414
00:28:25,870 --> 00:28:29,774
and Clifton, do not care

415
00:28:29,808 --> 00:28:32,877
very much about what the rest of the world
thinks.

416
00:28:32,911 --> 00:28:37,048
Number one and number two,
they feel they're basically free

417
00:28:37,082 --> 00:28:40,452
to do as they want in places like Gaza.

418
00:28:40,518 --> 00:28:46,324
Places like Syria, places like Lebanon,
and of course, the West Bank as well.

419
00:28:46,524 --> 00:28:51,629
So Israel has lost control
and the lobby has lost

420
00:28:51,629 --> 00:28:54,999
control of the discourse
for all these reasons.

421
00:28:55,734 --> 00:28:58,870
And that situation
is not likely to change.

422
00:28:58,937 --> 00:29:02,807
Now, as I said to you before
with regard to policy.

423
00:29:02,841 --> 00:29:05,844
The policy has not changed.

424
00:29:05,877 --> 00:29:09,647
The United States remains firmly committed

425
00:29:09,647 --> 00:29:12,717
to supporting Israel unconditionally.

426
00:29:12,951 --> 00:29:15,353
This is no question on that front.

427
00:29:15,353 --> 00:29:18,990
So we have the situation today,

428
00:29:19,491 --> 00:29:23,995
which Eli and Ian
and do a brilliant job of describing,

429
00:29:23,995 --> 00:29:29,067
where the policy
and the discourse are out of sync.

430
00:29:29,267 --> 00:29:33,571
So the question then is
what is the lobby doing

431
00:29:34,272 --> 00:29:37,709
to number one,
try and rectify the discourse

432
00:29:37,809 --> 00:29:43,248
or rectify the problem that it faces
in terms of the discourse.

433
00:29:43,281 --> 00:29:45,250
And then number two.

434
00:29:45,250 --> 00:29:48,953
What is it trying to do to make sure

435
00:29:48,953 --> 00:29:54,192
that moving forward,
there's no change in American policy

436
00:29:54,259 --> 00:30:00,031
toward Israel, that the lobby and Israel
working together,

437
00:30:00,298 --> 00:30:05,670
continue to maintain a hammerlock on US
policy.

438
00:30:05,837 --> 00:30:09,007
Let's start
by talking about the discourse.

439
00:30:09,474 --> 00:30:13,411
And with regard to the discourse,

440
00:30:13,912 --> 00:30:19,284
really two things are happening here
that they describe in considerable detail.

441
00:30:19,450 --> 00:30:24,956
One has to do
with the definition of anti-Semitism.

442
00:30:25,323 --> 00:30:30,161
When Steve
and I wrote the book back in 2007,

443
00:30:30,295 --> 00:30:34,098
it was a pretty widespread understanding

444
00:30:34,098 --> 00:30:37,068
of what anti-Semitism was.

445
00:30:37,368 --> 00:30:39,170
And

446
00:30:40,271 --> 00:30:41,840
what's happened over time

447
00:30:41,840 --> 00:30:47,111
is the definition of anti-Semitism
has been broadened greatly.

448
00:30:47,478 --> 00:30:51,082
And today, the lobby

449
00:30:51,082 --> 00:30:54,652
and many others,
because of the power of the lobby

450
00:30:54,652 --> 00:30:58,323
to spread this idea, have this very loose

451
00:30:58,323 --> 00:31:02,093
definition of what anti-Semitism is.

452
00:31:02,093 --> 00:31:06,865
It's the IHRA definition you're 
saying to you.

453
00:31:06,898 --> 00:31:09,000
So what does IHRA mean?

454
00:31:09,000 --> 00:31:13,538
It's the International
Historical Remembrance Alliance,

455
00:31:13,872 --> 00:31:17,642
excuse me, the International Holocaust
Remembrance Alliance,

456
00:31:17,642 --> 00:31:22,847
International Holocaust Remembrance
Alliance, IHRA definition of anti-Semitism,

457
00:31:22,847 --> 00:31:28,653
and that IHRA definition of anti-Semitism
is very broad.

458
00:31:28,653 --> 00:31:33,324
And what it effectively means
is that criticism of Israel

459
00:31:33,324 --> 00:31:35,593
is seen as anti-Semitism.

460
00:31:35,593 --> 00:31:40,598
So anybody who is criticizing Israel
for its genocide in Gaza

461
00:31:40,598 --> 00:31:44,602
or its barbaric behavior in places
like the West Bank is

462
00:31:44,636 --> 00:31:49,173
said to be an anti-Semite,
according to this definition.

463
00:31:49,207 --> 00:31:54,479
So what the lobby has tried to do
by deploying this IHRA

464
00:31:54,512 --> 00:32:00,351
definition of anti-Semitism is make it
virtually impossible to criticize Israel

465
00:32:00,351 --> 00:32:05,790
without putting yourself in a position
where you're labeled an anti-Semite.

466
00:32:05,990 --> 00:32:10,328
When Steve Walt and I wrote our book,
we had a chapter

467
00:32:10,328 --> 00:32:15,600
called The Great Silencer, 
and we talked in that chapter

468
00:32:15,600 --> 00:32:20,638
about how the charge of anti-Semitism is
used as the great silencer.

469
00:32:20,672 --> 00:32:24,842
And of course, Eli and Ian
are talking about exactly that.

470
00:32:24,842 --> 00:32:29,013
And they are dealing with this

471
00:32:29,047 --> 00:32:32,717
IHRA definition, which is a very important
part of the story,

472
00:32:32,717 --> 00:32:36,754
which was not part of the story
when we wrote our book.

473
00:32:37,188 --> 00:32:43,027
So that's the first tool
that the lobby uses to combat

474
00:32:44,429 --> 00:32:46,731
criticism of Israel.

475
00:32:46,731 --> 00:32:49,667
In effect,
the aim here is to make criticism

476
00:32:49,667 --> 00:32:54,172
of Israel anti-Semitic
and therefore silence critics.

477
00:32:54,205 --> 00:32:59,177
The second thing that's happened
is that the lobby has used the government

478
00:32:59,243 --> 00:33:02,680
to crack down on

479
00:33:02,747 --> 00:33:08,052
anyone who criticizes Israel,
and the best example of that

480
00:33:08,052 --> 00:33:12,290
were the protests that took place
all across college and university

481
00:33:12,357 --> 00:33:16,828
campuses in the United States
in the spring of 2024.

482
00:33:16,961 --> 00:33:20,631
Remember, after October 7th, 2023,

483
00:33:20,698 --> 00:33:24,736
after the Hamas attack into Israel.

484
00:33:24,869 --> 00:33:30,274
Israel went on the offensive and
eventually ended up executing a genocide.

485
00:33:30,274 --> 00:33:36,147
And unsurprisingly, by the spring of 2024,
there were large scale,

486
00:33:36,147 --> 00:33:40,551
if not massive, protests on campuses
all across the United States.

487
00:33:41,219 --> 00:33:44,856
The lobby went to work
and put enormous pressure

488
00:33:44,856 --> 00:33:50,061
on the US government
to shut down those protests.

489
00:33:50,094 --> 00:33:52,630
And by the way,
this was not the Trump administration.

490
00:33:52,630 --> 00:33:54,298
It was the Biden administration.

491
00:33:54,298 --> 00:33:57,468
And the Biden administration
played ball with the lobby,

492
00:33:57,468 --> 00:34:01,439
and those protests were shut down.

493
00:34:01,439 --> 00:34:06,844
And if you go to university
or college campuses today,

494
00:34:07,211 --> 00:34:10,815
you'll see remarkably little evidence

495
00:34:10,815 --> 00:34:13,818
of any criticism of Israel.

496
00:34:13,818 --> 00:34:18,156
It's really quite amazing
how good the lobby and the government

497
00:34:18,156 --> 00:34:22,493
working together as a tag team,
have been at shutting down

498
00:34:22,493 --> 00:34:27,698
criticism of Israel
on college and university campuses.

499
00:34:28,433 --> 00:34:33,237
And of course, this is linked in part
to using that broad definition

500
00:34:33,271 --> 00:34:36,274
of anti-Semitism purveyed by the lobby,

501
00:34:36,274 --> 00:34:41,079
because if people on college campuses
set out to protest

502
00:34:41,112 --> 00:34:45,283
Israeli behavior and criticizes
Israel or criticize the lobby

503
00:34:45,349 --> 00:34:49,921
or criticize the US-Israel relationship,
what happens very quickly

504
00:34:50,455 --> 00:34:52,990
is that the government defines that

505
00:34:52,990 --> 00:34:56,494
as anti-Semitism and goes to work.

506
00:34:56,594 --> 00:34:59,630
So this is how the lobby has been

507
00:34:59,630 --> 00:35:02,867
trying to police the discourse.

508
00:35:03,201 --> 00:35:07,038
Or, to put it slightly differently,

509
00:35:07,038 --> 00:35:11,642
to sort of recapture
control of the discourse.

510
00:35:12,310 --> 00:35:14,612
The fact is, it's failed.

511
00:35:14,612 --> 00:35:16,447
There's just no question about that.

512
00:35:16,447 --> 00:35:21,052
The lobby has been unable to recapture

513
00:35:21,252 --> 00:35:24,355
control of the discourse.

514
00:35:24,355 --> 00:35:26,724
And the main reason is the internet.

515
00:35:26,724 --> 00:35:33,231
It's just almost impossible in the age
of the internet to control the discourse

516
00:35:33,231 --> 00:35:39,237
the way the lobby once did
before the coming of the internet.

517
00:35:40,204 --> 00:35:41,239
Then there's the question

518
00:35:41,239 --> 00:35:44,408
of policy
what's going on at the policy level.

519
00:35:44,408 --> 00:35:47,411
And there Clifton and

520
00:35:48,446 --> 00:35:49,714
Lustic have a

521
00:35:49,714 --> 00:35:52,617
Very interesting story to tell.

522
00:35:52,617 --> 00:35:55,620
First of all, they talk about

523
00:35:55,686 --> 00:36:01,092
the growth of plutocracy
in the United States,

524
00:36:01,292 --> 00:36:05,029
the fact
that we have a large number of plutocrats,

525
00:36:05,196 --> 00:36:11,402
some of whom are Jewish,
and those Jewish plutocrats are willing

526
00:36:11,435 --> 00:36:15,907
to expand huge amounts of money
to influence elections,

527
00:36:16,307 --> 00:36:21,846
both at the congressional level
and at the presidential level.

528
00:36:22,346 --> 00:36:28,319
And not only that, not only do
we have this plutocrat class

529
00:36:28,319 --> 00:36:32,056
that includes wealthy Jews
who are deeply committed to Israel,

530
00:36:32,890 --> 00:36:38,029
but we also had a decision.

531
00:36:38,095 --> 00:36:41,499
A Supreme Court decision was made in 2010.

532
00:36:42,233 --> 00:36:45,336
This is the Citizens United decision

533
00:36:45,770 --> 00:36:48,806
that basically allowed individuals.

534
00:36:48,839 --> 00:36:54,378
In other words, these wealthy plutocrats
to spend almost as much money

535
00:36:54,378 --> 00:36:57,815
as they want on congressional

536
00:36:57,815 --> 00:37:00,818
and on presidential elections.

537
00:37:00,918 --> 00:37:05,523
So you have this situation
where someone like Miriam Adelson,

538
00:37:06,157 --> 00:37:09,961
who is both an Israeli citizen
and an American citizen

539
00:37:09,961 --> 00:37:14,165
and who clearly identifies
more with Israel than the United States,

540
00:37:14,198 --> 00:37:18,803
according to Donald Trump, 
gave him an enormous

541
00:37:18,803 --> 00:37:24,575
sum of money
which helped him to get reelected in 2024.

542
00:37:24,675 --> 00:37:30,314
And of course, Miriam Adelson
was not the only Jewish plutocrat

543
00:37:30,348 --> 00:37:33,351
who was supporting Donald Trump.

544
00:37:33,718 --> 00:37:39,390
But the more general point here
is that in the United States of America,

545
00:37:39,390 --> 00:37:43,494
we have a political system
where to get elected.

546
00:37:43,527 --> 00:37:49,367
You need a lot of money, and
to get reelected, you need a lot of money.

547
00:37:49,400 --> 00:37:55,706
And if you have plutocrats
who can spend unlimited sums of money

548
00:37:56,173 --> 00:37:59,510
helping people get elected,

549
00:37:59,577 --> 00:38:02,880
who are pro-Israel in their view,

550
00:38:02,880 --> 00:38:08,119
and can help defeat candidates
or incumbents

551
00:38:08,119 --> 00:38:12,556
who are viewed as anti-Israel,
in their view,

552
00:38:12,957 --> 00:38:17,962
you're going to quickly reach a situation
where

553
00:38:18,496 --> 00:38:21,365
most people on Capitol Hill

554
00:38:21,365 --> 00:38:26,837
and almost all presidents
are going to be afraid to cross the lobby

555
00:38:26,837 --> 00:38:31,442
and will do pretty much
what the lobby wants.

556
00:38:31,442 --> 00:38:37,481
And of course, you saw this with Joe
Biden, and you see this with Donald Trump.

557
00:38:37,548 --> 00:38:42,386
Neither Biden
nor Trump dare to cross the lobby.

558
00:38:42,386 --> 00:38:48,693
And this has been true, of course,
for a long time in American politics.

559
00:38:48,726 --> 00:38:52,029
And the reason is today

560
00:38:52,930 --> 00:38:57,435
that you have all these plutocrats

561
00:38:57,635 --> 00:39:03,641
who are deeply committed to Israel
and can spend endless amounts of money

562
00:39:03,641 --> 00:39:06,644
because of the 2010 Citizens

563
00:39:06,644 --> 00:39:10,848
United decision by the Supreme Court.

564
00:39:11,349 --> 00:39:14,218
So what's the bottom line here?

565
00:39:14,218 --> 00:39:18,756
The bottom line here
is that since Steve and I wrote our book,

566
00:39:18,856 --> 00:39:23,594
the discourse about Israel has changed
drastically.

567
00:39:23,594 --> 00:39:27,331
The public discourse about Israel
has changed drastically.

568
00:39:27,365 --> 00:39:31,202
And as I said before,
that's due in large part to the internet,

569
00:39:31,202 --> 00:39:36,440
coupled with Israeli behavior
and how Israel thinks about itself.

570
00:39:36,474 --> 00:39:40,711
Those various factors have led
to this fundamental change

571
00:39:40,711 --> 00:39:45,216
in the discourse,
but the policy has not changed.

572
00:39:45,483 --> 00:39:50,921
The lobby is still able

573
00:39:50,955 --> 00:39:55,559
to influence policy
in ways that the United States

574
00:39:55,593 --> 00:39:59,163
maintains
unconditional support for Israel.

575
00:39:59,530 --> 00:40:05,536
So the big question moving forward,
and this will be a question that 20 years

576
00:40:05,536 --> 00:40:10,875
from now, the successors to Clifton
and Lustick will write write about.

577
00:40:10,908 --> 00:40:14,278
The question is how successful

578
00:40:14,278 --> 00:40:19,550
will the lobby be in the years
or in the years ahead

579
00:40:20,151 --> 00:40:23,921
at maintaining support for Israel?

580
00:40:24,054 --> 00:40:27,725
Unequivocal support
for Israel at the policy level,

581
00:40:27,958 --> 00:40:32,696
when in fact support for Israel

582
00:40:32,730 --> 00:40:39,737
has significantly deteriorated
at the popular level.

583
00:40:39,870 --> 00:40:42,840
This is really the big question
moving forward.

584
00:40:42,840 --> 00:40:46,110
This was not a question
that Steve and I faced when we wrote.

585
00:40:46,110 --> 00:40:47,812
I want to emphasize that again.

586
00:40:47,812 --> 00:40:51,048
When Steve and I wrote,
the lobby was pretty much in charge

587
00:40:51,048 --> 00:40:54,351
of the discourse
and pretty much in charge of policy.

588
00:40:54,351 --> 00:40:56,587
But that has changed.

589
00:40:56,587 --> 00:40:59,590
Lobby has lost its ability
to control the discourse.

590
00:40:59,590 --> 00:41:02,626
And again,
what you want to think about moving

591
00:41:02,626 --> 00:41:05,729
forward is what effect

592
00:41:06,130 --> 00:41:09,934
this will have on policy, on US policy

593
00:41:09,934 --> 00:41:14,071
toward Israel in the years ahead.

594
00:41:14,238 --> 00:41:18,409
So on that note, I will conclude,
and I just want to say again,

595
00:41:18,409 --> 00:41:24,081
I think that people
who are interested in US

596
00:41:24,081 --> 00:41:29,954
Middle East policy, who are interested in
how the lobby influences that policy,

597
00:41:30,154 --> 00:41:33,757
you should definitely go out
and read this new

598
00:41:33,757 --> 00:41:40,331
book by Ian Lustig and Eli Clifton,
because it's a superb book

599
00:41:40,364 --> 00:41:44,568
and it says all sorts of interesting

600
00:41:44,568 --> 00:41:50,875
and important things about the lobby
and about Israel,

601
00:41:51,008 --> 00:41:56,847
and about the effect
the lobby is having on US democracy.

602
00:41:56,881 --> 00:42:00,818
This is not a small issue,
and this is an issue

603
00:42:00,818 --> 00:42:05,189
that I have not dwelled on today,
but which these authors

604
00:42:05,189 --> 00:42:09,927
spend a lot of time
talking about in their new book.

605
00:42:10,394 --> 00:42:12,997
On that note,
let me close and say thank you

606
00:42:12,997 --> 00:42:17,735
for watching this episode
and I look forward to the next episode.

